            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This looks like a result of e3d13e2c89a9dfda51c69c825360d1fe5be0e322 which (accidentally) started forcing full two-step completion on LSP triggers. This is not correct and it should force only LSP completion without fallback (which is probably the culprit here as default `<C-n>` fallback is synchronous).\r\n\r\nThis particular issue should be fixed on latest `main`. Would you mind checking with your use case?",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This looks like a result of <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/commit/e3d13e2c89a9dfda51c69c825360d1fe5be0e322/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/commit/e3d13e2c89a9dfda51c69c825360d1fe5be0e322\"><tt>e3d13e2</tt></a> which (accidentally) started forcing full two-step completion on LSP triggers. This is not correct and it should force only LSP completion without fallback (which is probably the culprit here as default <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-n&gt;</code> fallback is synchronous).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This particular issue should be fixed on latest <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code>. Would you mind checking with your use case?</p>",
            "bodyText": "This looks like a result of e3d13e2 which (accidentally) started forcing full two-step completion on LSP triggers. This is not correct and it should force only LSP completion without fallback (which is probably the culprit here as default <C-n> fallback is synchronous).\nThis particular issue should be fixed on latest main. Would you mind checking with your use case?",
